    <data name="StoriesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What testers write to us</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story1Quote" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>I deleted my old app the day it asked for my email. Liora opened and asked one thing: when did your last period start?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story1Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Hannah K.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story1Meta" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Gothenburg, testing since September</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story2Quote" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>My cycles run anywhere from 26 to 35 days. Seeing a window instead of one date is the first time an app has been honest with me.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story2Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Nasrin A.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story2Meta" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Malmö, testing since October</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story3Quote" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>I made the PDF summary in the waiting room and showed my doctor the phone. Nothing went through anyone's server first.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story3Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Chloé M.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Story3Meta" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Lyon, testing since September</value>
    </data>
    <data name="FaqKicker" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Questions</value>
    </data>
    <data name="FaqTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Answered plainly</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq1Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Is Liora a medical device?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq1Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>No. Liora is a diary that makes predictions. It can't diagnose anything and it isn't a method of contraception. If something about your cycle worries you, talk to a doctor or a midwife.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq2Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Can you see what I log?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq2Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>No. Without backup, nothing leaves your phone. With backup on, we store a file that only your recovery phrase can open.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq3Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What if I lose my phone?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq3Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Without backup, your data goes with the phone and we can't bring it back. With backup, install Liora on the new iPhone and enter your 12-word recovery phrase.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq4Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What will it cost?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq4Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The beta is free. After 1.0, logging, predictions and reminders stay free. Any paid extras will be optional, and the app will show their price before anything changes.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq5Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>When is Android coming?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq5Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>In spring 2027. Join the list and we'll send one email, the day it's on Google Play.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq6Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Can I export or delete everything?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq6Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Yes. Settings has a PDF summary, a CSV file of every entry, and one button that erases the app's data and your backup.</value>
    </data>
